s a\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:616:          (stack-restore vm\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:617:                         (values/payload f)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:701:      ;; as a value: the register payload under the shared tag the B0\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:712:      ;; :park -- the engine records the payload under a fresh parked id,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:719:      ;; continuation named by the operand, through this machine's restore\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:725:                                    stack-restore))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:740:   loop with this machine's step function and its restore bound into the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:747:                   #(engine/resume-from-run-queue % stack-restore)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:765:          (engine/scheduler-round this stack-restore)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:809:  (link-format [_] {:format format-tag, :contract vm/stack-contract})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:827:                :contract vm/stack-contract}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:828:  (image-identity [_ image] (dcode/image-hash image))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:829:  (image-holds? [_ image segment] (= segment (dcode/image-hash image)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:830:  (attach-module [vm image] (attach-image vm image vm/stack-contract))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:869:  ;; A register payload (a wait, ready or parked entry, or a reified\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:4:   `{:bodies [...], :instructions [...]}` under contract version 4\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:5:   (the \\\"r2\\\" contract).\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:28:   effects tier, connecting to `yin.vm.engine` via `register-restore` and\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:46:   hash         ; R of segment (yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:73:  \"The model tag every register payload carries as `:format`.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:139:             :images [[(rcode/register-hash empty-image) 0 0]]\n2:  \"Universal Continuation Format, Phase 1: code identity and safepoints\n15:     it is interpreted under is `contract-stamp`. `canonicalize` bundles\n18:   - S7.4 safepoints. `safepoints` derives, from the canonical vector\n19:     alone, the static half of the safepoint map a foreign engine\n38:(def contract-stamp\n203:(defn code-address\n213:   :yin.k/contract contract-stamp}`; otherwise the `refusal` map the\n227:       :yin.code/hash (code-address v),\n228:       :yin.k/contract contract-stamp})\n246:   safepoints of S7.4.1. `:call` is parking because the operator may be a\n248:   is a step, not a safepoint (it reifies and continues).\"\n274:  \"S7.4.1's safepoint kinds, by parking mnemonic -- the static\n275:   possibilities of `:yin.safepoint/kinds`, per the owner ruling in\n349:(defn safepoints\n350:  \"The static safepoint map of one canonical vector (S7.4.2): one entry per\n363:              {:yin.safepoint/at pc,\n364:               :yin.safepoint/pc (inc pc),\n365:               :yin.safepoint/kinds (get parking-kinds (nth t 0)),\n366:               :yin.safepoint/stack-effect (stack-effect t),\n367:               :yin.safepoint/lexically-required\n372:(defn safepoint-table\n373:  \"`safepoints` published per segment, keyed by the code's address and the\n375:  ([v] (safepoint-table v :yin.vm.semantic/reference))\n377:   {:yin.safepoint/segment (code-address v),\n378:    :yin.safepoint/engine engine,\n379:    :yin.safepoint/safepoints (safepoints v)}))\n382:(defn safepoint-at\n383:  \"The static safepoint entry whose canonical resume pc is `pc`, or the\n384:   S7.9 `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` outcome naming the pc.\"\n386:  (or (some #(when (= pc (:yin.safepoint/pc %)) %) (safepoints v))\n387:      {:yin.k/status :yin.k/not-at-safepoint, :yin.k/pc pc}))\n402:  \"The lexically require